    "title": {
     "en": "A short story"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Meena saw an old iron gate turn brown and thought, \"Such changes take years.\"\n\"Some changes are slow,\" said her teacher."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "reversible",
     "permanent",
     "weathering"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Some changes are reversible, like melting and freezing ice. Others are permanent, like burning paper or cooking food.\nNot all changes are desirable. Rusting spoils iron, food going bad wastes it and forest fires harm nature. Some changes are useful, like cooking and making curd.\nSlow natural changes include weathering of rocks, rusting and the growth of plants."
    }
